# Extend FakeCheckPro Backend Architecture

This plan covers extending the existing FastAPI backend to support URL detection, Image OCR detection, and Prediction History while ensuring a single ML prediction pipeline.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **OCR Dependency**: Tesseract OCR must be installed on the host system to run the Image feature. The path will be configurable via `.env`.
> - **Database Segregation**: Per requirements, prediction history will be stored in a separate `prediction_history.db` SQLite database (with future PostgreSQL compatibility in mind), although user data exists in `fakecheckpro.db`.
> - **Dependencies**: New dependencies will be added to `requirements.txt`: `trafilatura` (URL extraction), `pytesseract` (OCR), `Pillow` (image processing), `python-multipart` (file uploads), `httpx` (async URL fetching), and `dnspython` (for SSRF protection).

## Open Questions
- Should `python-multipart` be installed for image uploads (standard for FastAPI)? Assuming yes.
- Should we use synchronous `requests` or asynchronous `httpx` for URL fetching? I propose `httpx` for better async integration in FastAPI, alongside standard socket/DNS checks for SSRF.
- Should the `prediction_history.db` share the same SQLAlchemy Base/engine setup conceptually, or be totally distinct? I will create a distinct configuration block for it in `app/database/history_db.py` to keep it separate.

